# The tests/hooks/fixtures/*/root/proc/<pid>/exe symlinks are test
# fixtures that emulate real /proc/<pid>/exe entries for the DNS-backend
# detection test suite (tests/hooks/test-survey-fixtures.sh) -- on a real
# system /proc/<pid>/exe always resolves to an absolute path, so a
# relative target here would misrepresent exactly what is being tested.
#
# Left unqualified (no per-file context) on purpose: lintian renders and
# matches a pointed tag's context differently depending on its own
# version -- e.g. Focal's lintian (2.62.x, pre-dating the
# Lintian::Hint::Pointed rewrite) prints/matches "<path> -> <target>",
# while current lintian (post-rewrite) prints/matches
# "<target> [<path>]". A context string written for one format silently
# fails to match under the other, so the warning survives on whichever
# release ships the format the override wasn't written for. Since these
# four fixture symlinks are the only source of this tag, dropping the
# context suppresses all of them unconditionally on every lintian
# version instead of chasing its context format per release.
ipsec-tools source: absolute-symbolic-link-target-in-source

